`crt_router_multiple_test_payloads` also uses `tool_name`/`arguments` when constructing `ToolPreInvokePayload`, but the payload model fields are `name` and `args`. This will fail validation (missing `name`) and should be updated to use the correct field names.
```suggestion
            name="test_tool_a",
            args={"query": "simple search"}
        ),
        ToolPreInvokePayload(
            name="test_tool_b",
            args={"data": [1, 2, 3], "operation": "analyze"}
        ),
        ToolPreInvokePayload(
            name="test_tool_c",
            args={}  # No arguments
```
